<title>CANADA: Canada minister says GM strike not his bailiwick.</title>
<headline>Canada minister says GM strike not his bailiwick.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Labour Minister Alfonso Gagliano said on Thursday it was not up to him to intervene in the strike at General Motors Corp's Canadian unit.</p>
<p>&quot;It's up to my provincial colleague to intervene (if he decides to),&quot; Gagliano told reporters at Parliament.</p>
<p>He encouraged the two sides to resolve their differences at the bargaining table. About 15,500 GM unionized workers in Ontario and Quebec went on strike late on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
